(E) Remark 4.5: C_{k,M}, M = n = lambda (k-2)/(lambda-1): a consistent parity ties the coin
  k=20 lambda=2   : n=M=36, parity length 38 = (lambda k - 2)/(lambda - 1) = 38.0; J(parity) = J(coin) = 76.0; P[A invertible] = 0.2888; bound (lambda k + delta_n)/(lambda-1) - length = 5.50e-06 (= log2(1+2^(2-k))/(lambda-1) = 5.50e-06)
  k=20 lambda=3/2 : n=M=54, parity length 56 = (lambda k - 2)/(lambda - 1) = 56.0; J(parity) = J(coin) = 84.0; P[A invertible] = 0.2888; bound (lambda k + delta_n)/(lambda-1) - length = 1.10e-05 (= log2(1+2^(2-k))/(lambda-1) = 1.10e-05)
  k=30 lambda=3   : n=M=42, parity length 44 = (lambda k - 2)/(lambda - 1) = 44.0; J(parity) = J(coin) = 132.0; P[A invertible] = 0.2888; bound (lambda k + delta_n)/(lambda-1) - length = 2.69e-09 (= log2(1+2^(2-k))/(lambda-1) = 2.69e-09)
  k=16 lambda=5/4 : n=M=70, parity length 72 = (lambda k - 2)/(lambda - 1) = 72.0; J(parity) = J(coin) = 90.0; P[A invertible] = 0.2888; bound (lambda k + delta_n)/(lambda-1) - length = 3.52e-04 (= log2(1+2^(2-k))/(lambda-1) = 3.52e-04)
  k=40 lambda=2   : n=M=76, parity length 78 = (lambda k - 2)/(lambda - 1) = 78.0; J(parity) = J(coin) = 156.0; P[A invertible] = 0.2888; bound (lambda k + delta_n)/(lambda-1) - length = 5.24e-12 (= log2(1+2^(2-k))/(lambda-1) = 5.25e-12)
  On {A invertible} exactly one parity is consistent, so delta_n = log2(1/4 + 2^-k) and the MAP set is {coin, parity}.
